  "protocol": "Whole function replacement with runner-owned identical AST dependency closures; first attempt plus at most one fresh independent repair using only the same prompt, raw first reply and first rejection. Arm order rotates by task; one fresh fork-none Codex agent per cell. No subject sees tests or reference. No tool/test access beyond reading assigned prompt and writing assigned reply.",
  "selectionRule": "Candidate eligible only if total accepted count after at most one repair is no lower than each legacy arm, no application group loses accepted count, and visible payload tokens per accepted edit decrease vs canonical for each tokenizer. Report one-shot separately, all failures and per-group/arm outcomes regardless. Narrow evidence; no universal superiority or final frontend claim.",
  "tokenAccounting": "o200k_base and cl100k_base counts of actual assigned prompt, returned source payload, and supplied repair prompt. Excludes platform/system/tool framing, hidden reasoning, billed usage and other provider overhead, which collaboration does not expose. Wall clock is orchestration elapsed, not inference-only latency. Whole-function protocol excludes potential line-edit savings.",
